Z||000001||AkursedX||05-20-2001||09:51 PM||||You know, not to take away anything from the ability of Allen Iverson, because he is one phenominal player, but to be honest, I just can't stand him, like many other professional athletes.  <BR>I am a former college football player and I always have taken a lot of pride in being an athlete.  But the term "athlete" doesn't seem to mean what it used to.  I mean being a great player is one thing, but there is so much more to being an athlete.  There is your behavior on and off the court, and most importantly, respect of your teammates and of your advesaries.<BR>When I played, I was the type of person who never talked a word of trash, addressed the officals as "sir", and always gave a hand to help other players up, whether they were on my team or not.  It's so sad to see this type of attitude disappearing in pro-sports.<BR>The only real pro football "idol" I had was the late Walter Payton.  To me, he exemplified everything an athlete should be.  He played every down like it was his last.  You never saw him run out of bounds, he was always willing to sacrifice his body for the game.  He was also a gentleman and good standing citizen off the field as well.  <BR>The only sport i really watch anymore is autoracing, and that isn't even really perfect, but it is alot better than the 4 major sports (NFL NBA NHL MLB)  <P>So basically what I'm saying is, yes, the athletes are great players, but are they really great people??  <P>Note:  I know not all athletes are like this, but it's just how I feel about how sports are becoming.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by AkursedX (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||05-20-2001||10:03 PM||||players just want the money, theres no love for the game anymore. "Yeah man, I grew up Atlanta, I lived my entire life in Atlanta, I wanted to play in Atlanta, but hey, Florida offered me .05 million $$ more... show me the money babe, show me the money".. that there is bull. I would not have a player playing for me that would think like that. Whats sad, most of todays sports ppl are like that. They all think about the money and not the game. <P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
